From dbed3ca6da809cfd6cbe1dcd07b841edbeac2ef7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:06:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] A Rogue's afterimage keeps its own colour, so its pale ghost
 and violet shade show

Basin Battle. The aura tint publish (aura_visual::apply_aura_tint) rewrites every RigSkin's tint
slot each frame, and an afterimage copy is a RigSkin with no aura of its own, so the colour
spawn_afterimages gave it went back to none on the next frame: the perfect dodge's copy, meant to
be lit pale blue-white (patch 0112), drew as the dark-clad body itself, a dark smear. A copy made
with a light (the thirty-fourth round's lit tint) or a stand-in (Afterimage's shade) now carries
OwnTint, which the publish skips; a freed slot is still cleared by RigSkin's hook. A flurry's
copies (Bladestorm) are as they were. No new round: the same AI line now draws as it was meant to.
